        "title": "Near-degenerate competing magnetic orders in EuAgAs: a tunable route to altermagnetism",
        "authors": "Mohamed El Gazzah, Daniel Kaplan, Zachary Morgan, Abhijeet Nayak Resham Regmi, Sk Jamaluddin, Huibo Cao, Igor I. Mazin, Nirmal J. Ghimire",
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.16242v1",
        "source": "arxiv:cond-mat.str-el",
        "published": "2026-05-15",
        "arxiv_id": "2605.16242v1",
        "is_stm": false,
        "is_premium": false,
        "score": 3,
        "score_reason": "仅命中磁性拓扑材料方向（+1分），但无STM/STS实验手段，与实验室核心研究方向（涡旋、超导、界面等）无直接关联。",
        "summary_cn": "本研究通过中子衍射实验发现EuAgAs基态为q=(0,0,½)反铁磁序，与先前理论预测的共线交变磁态不符。DFT计算表明铁磁和交变磁构型仅分别高出基态0.11和0.40 meV/f.u.，存在近简并竞争。非海森堡双二次耦合稳定了观察到的反铁磁相，而静水压约14 GPa可驱动至交变磁相，为拓扑交变磁性提供了可调控平台。",
        "abstract_excerpt": "Altermagnets (AMs) have recently emerged as a distinct magnetic class bridging central features of ferromagnets (FMs) and antiferromagnets (AFMs)... Our neutron diffraction experiments reveal that the bulk ground state adopts a \\(\\mathbf{q} = (0,0,\\tfrac{1}{2})\\) AFM structure... Systematic DFT calculations, however, uncover a remarkable near-degeneracy among competing magnetic orders: the FM and AM configurations lie only \\(0.11\\) and \\(0.40~\\text{meV/f.u.}\\) above the AFM ground state, respectively.",
